  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nA dry forecast with the only shot at measurable rainfall coming\ntonight into Sunday in the West Virginia mountains. There will \nbe a lot more clouds in Pennsylvania Sunday than today. Eastern \nOhio should be able to stay in the clear from the system passing\nthrough the mid Atlantic. A second moisture starved front \ncrosses Sunday night into Monday, which will reinforce cooler \nweather the first part of the week. In fact, the 0C isotherm at \n850mb gets into our northern counties Monday morning. \n\nThe rest of the work week features the column slowing warming \nand mid level heights building. High temps climb back above \nseasonal values with 70s common outside of the higher elevations\nThursday through next weekend. We may have a shot at our second\n80F degree day of the month next weekend with probs climbing \ninto the 30 percentile range and the forecast 50th percentile a \nfew degrees higher in most recent runs. \n\nFrost advisories are likely in the northeast and southeast\ncorners of our area Tuesday morning and perhaps Wednesday as \nwell. There is more confidence in Tuesday at sunrise given the \nlocation of the surface anticyclone. Probs of min temps less \nthan 37 degrees range from 45-80% in the aforementioned areas,\nwhile those numbers drop between 20-30% at daybreak Wednesday. \nThe mean first frost at Dubois airport is September 25th and the\n/late/ 90th percentile is October 9th, thus we are on the later\nside of climo this year.",
